---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="picoctf 2026"
    description="competing as sharon cyber. top 3% team globally."
>
    <a href="/" class="text-sm">return home </a>
    <header class="mb-4 mt-4">
        <h4 class="text-sm text-gray-500">mar 2026</h4>
        <h1 class="mb-4">picoctf 2026</h1>
        <p>competing as sharon cyber. top 3% team globally.</p>
        <div
            class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-2 my-4 font-mono text-sm text-gray-500 lowercase"
        >
            <span class="rounded border border-[#333] px-2 py-0.5">ctfs</span>
            <span class="rounded border border-[#333] px-2 py-0.5"
                >cryptography</span
            >
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 text-sm">
            <a href="https://github.com/smst/tetragon" target="_blank">
                github ↗
            </a>
        </div>
    </header>

    <article>
        <hr />
        <h3>debrief</h3>
        <p>
            <a href="https://learn.cylabacademy.org/teams/17496" target="_blank"
                >Our team
            </a> closed out picoCTF 2026 with 13,500 of 14,500 available points, placing
            us in the top 3% of teams globally. We struggled to solve the most difficult
            reverse engineering and web exploitation challenges (JITFP and paper-2,
            respectively), but we were able to solve every other challenge in the
            competition.
        </p>
        <p>
            I found two cryptography challenges particularly interesting. One
            makes use of a sloppy weakness in a particular implementation of
            RSA, and the other involved abusing lattice-based cryptography.
        </p>
        <hr />
        <h3>writeup: clusterrsa</h3>
        <p>Traditional RSA implementations rely on a modulus N = p * q.</p>
        <hr />
        <h3>writeup: NotTRUe</h3>
        <hr />
        <h3>outcome</h3>
        <hr />
        <div class="flex gap-4 text-sm">
            <a href="https://github.com/smst/tetragon" target="_blank">
                github ↗
            </a>
            <a href="/">return home </a>
        </div>
    </article>
</Layout>
